WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:03.620
Insects are a common fear among humans.

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:08.940
Evolutionarily, certain bugs are notorious
for spreading disease and in some cases even

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.380
being deadly.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:15.530
Arachnids like the Brown Recluse and Brazilian
Wandering Spider hold venoms that are extremely

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:19.000
painful or deadly in high enough dosages.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.160
Wasps and Hornets exist to defend their territory
and sting anything that gets close to them.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:29.000
Mosquitoes have been responsible for spreading
diseases throughout history - yellow fever,

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.150
malaria, zika virus, and West Nile virus to
name of a few.

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:36.930
However, what’s less commonly discussed
are ticks.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:41.710
They are similar to mosquitos, they latch
onto mammals and consume their blood by use

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:43.430
of a thin needle like mouth.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:49.460
They are also responsible for countless diseases,
the most infamous being Lyme Disease.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:54.930
These animals are parasitic in nature and
depend on mammals like humans for sustenance.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:59.830
Human beings are social creatures and because
of our behavior, it’s been made pretty easy

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:05.250
for us to make friends, find relationships,
connect with our parents, or do well in the

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.250
workplace.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:11.610
The ability for humans to find these connections
so easily allowed us to become the dominant

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:13.420
species on Earth.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:17.659
Without this ability, human beings would not
be in the place we are currently.

00:01:17.659 --> 00:01:23.020
Today, you may have gone out with a few friends,
spoke to your loved ones, or said hi to someone

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:24.170
on the street.

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:29.070
Imagine if these attempts to continue human
connection were instead met with silence,

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.630
blank stares, and disgust.

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:37.470
Well in the world of the SCP Foundation, this
fantasy is a reality for a few unlucky people

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:43.560
who ran into some uncontained anomalies before
the SCP Foundation could properly intervene.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:49.380
It was a mildly breezy summer day, perfect
for a picnic or relaxing outside with a refreshing

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:50.380
beverage.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:54.860
The weather was ideal and Daniel Arnoldson
was up bright and early hoping to take full

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:55.860
advantage of it.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:02:02.220
It had been weeks of what felt like an infinite
heatwave making long periods of daylight unbearable,

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:08.550
so Daniel and his wife, Eliza, were itching
to get a nice day outside, and now it came.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:12.879
After going over some ideas, they decided
on taking a nice hike through the nearby trail

00:02:12.879 --> 00:02:13.879
in the mountains.

00:02:13.879 --> 00:02:19.599
They began packing their backpacks: bear spray,
granola, water, and rain clothes in case this

00:02:19.599 --> 00:02:23.170
weather turned its back on the people who
were basking in its glory.

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:27.830
They also brought some picnic supplies for
when they reached the summit of the mountain.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:32.279
The car ride to the hiking trail was uneventful,
but the couple was happy.

00:02:32.279 --> 00:02:34.890
They were the epitome of high school sweethearts.

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:38.590
The two had been dating since their freshman
year of high school and it was practically

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:40.340
love at first sight.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.900
Dan and Eliza were almost inseparable.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.499
They spent every hour with each other and
never got bored of each other’s presence.

00:02:47.499 --> 00:02:52.340
They went to every school dance together and
even wore matching outfits every time - Aww…how

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:53.760
cute right?

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:58.340
- There was always something to talk about,
always something to laugh about, and they

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:00.760
never even had a real argument.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:05.599
They went to the same college to stay close,
and got married right after graduation.

00:03:05.599 --> 00:03:10.680
It was meant to be, Dan and Eliza were seemingly
perfect together in every way.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:15.379
And to be out of the house with bearable weather
was making them even more happy.

00:03:15.379 --> 00:03:19.409
They arrived at the start of the trail and
began their trek in the beautiful weather.

00:03:19.409 --> 00:03:24.239
It was long and it was tiring, but with each
other at their sides, they encouraged themselves

00:03:24.239 --> 00:03:26.409
to finish it and have their picnic.

00:03:26.409 --> 00:03:28.430
Eventually, they made it to the top.

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:33.339
Dan, who was more tired than Eliza, left picnic
set-up duties to her and took a seat in the

00:03:33.339 --> 00:03:34.339
grass.

00:03:34.339 --> 00:03:37.390
His exhaustion got the better of him, and
he laid down.

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:41.560
It seems the couple forgot one important item:
bug repellent.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:44.719
I guess they’re not so perfect after all
huh?

00:03:44.719 --> 00:03:50.059
As soon as Daniel laid himself onto the grass,
a small, almost invisible tick latched itself

00:03:50.059 --> 00:03:51.489
onto the back of his neck.

00:03:51.489 --> 00:03:55.859
He didn’t notice it, and sat up as soon
as the picnic mat was placed down and moved

00:03:55.859 --> 00:03:56.859
onto it.

00:03:56.859 --> 00:04:00.010
They shared a nice meal, and sat for some
time.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:05.319
As the sun began to set, the couple made their
way back down the mountain and returned home,

00:04:05.319 --> 00:04:08.639
now with their new, unknown visitor, the tick.

00:04:08.639 --> 00:04:11.540
The next morning, something changed in Eliza.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:14.930
It was a monday, so Daniel had to get up early
for work.

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:19.850
Normally, he’s met with a groggy kiss and
a sluggish “good morning” from his wife,

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:21.970
but this day, he didn’t get that.

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:22.970
Dan brushed it off.

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:25.270
“She was probably just tired from the hike.”

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:27.730
He thought to himself, and headed to work.

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:30.660
The day went by the same as most work days.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:34.850
Putting in the hours, excited to get back
home to his lovely wife for a nice evening

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:36.610
of Netflix and chill.

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:39.830
But he returned to something he never expected
to see.

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:46.980
As he pulled into his driveway he saw all
of his belongings: shirts, pants, shoes, books,

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:52.250
pieces of technology, even the gifts he bought
for Eliza - all left in a heaping pile on

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.380
the pavement outside of their house.

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:58.960
He was appalled, his heart began to race as
questions flooded his mind.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:00.760
“Did I do something wrong?”

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:01.990
“Did I say something hurtful?”

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:05.170
I thought she had a good time yesterday, what
happened?”

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:09.940
He frantically barged into the house and immediately
yelled for his wife: “Eliza!”

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:11.380
But there was no response.

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:14.460
“Eliza!” he cried again, but to no avail.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:18.320
Either she wasn’t home or he was being completely
ignored.

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:23.120
He ventured through the many rooms of his
home, looking for any sign of his wife.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:27.280
Dan found her in her office, and said her
name to her again.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:28.280
“Eliza?”

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:29.280
No response.

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:30.560
She didn’t even look at him.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:31.580
“What’s going on, Eliza?

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.420
Why aren’t you talking to me?”

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:34.500
He yelled at her.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.620
No response.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:39.390
He pushed Eliza’s desk out of the way and
stood in front of her, but was met with a

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:41.610
blank, forward facing stare.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:42.610
Nothing.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:45.210
She didn’t even seem to see him.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:49.810
Daniel went to touch his wife’s shoulder
and upon contact, her face turned to disgust

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:53.190
and she recoiled, but she still didn’t look
at him.

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:57.370
For the next five hours, Daniel tried his
hardest to get the smallest amount of acknowledgement

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:03.810
from his wife, but all he was met with was
silence, blank stares, and a face of disgust

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:05.710
whenever he went to touch her.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:09.240
Day turned to night as Daniel’s pleas to
his wife continued.

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:14.330
It went on for so long, that a nearby neighbor
called the police, and Daniel was arrested

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:17.450
and placed in a criminal psychiatric ward
for the time.

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:21.360
He stayed there for a few days, as police
interviewed Eliza.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:25.920
They asked her a number of questions regarding
Daniel, but she didn’t even know who Daniel

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:26.920
was.

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:31.740
She was shown pictures of them together, but
there was no sign of recognition from her,

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:34.460
she couldn’t even see him in the pictures.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:39.360
That is when the SCP Foundation agents embedded
in the local law enforcement sniffed out that

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:43.030
there was a potential anomaly involved in
this event.

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:47.820
The SCP Foundation agents wrangled oversight
away from the original police officers and

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:49.870
began their investigation.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:54.430
They interviewed Daniel, where he told them
the story of the hike and about the day after

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:55.430
it.

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:59.810
The SCP Foundation researchers, still posing
as police and medical professionals, were

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:00.810
stumped.

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:05.730
What could cause such a loving couple to detach
from one another like that, and why was Eliza

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:09.090
acting as if she couldn’t even see Daniel?

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:13.700
After a medical examination, the tick Dan
had been bitten by during the hike was found

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:15.400
to be still attached to him.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:19.520
It was removed, and Daniel was allowed to
go free from the psychiatric ward.

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:22.240
Sadly, Daniel went missing the next day.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:26.950
The following note was found in a diary he
began writing in since the start of the event:

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:28.430
“All alone.

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:29.480
Always alone.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:32.210
She couldn't see me, no matter what I did.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:34.060
She couldn't care.

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:35.570
I thought we were happy.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:39.860
Then one day, I come back home and all of
my stuff is out on the pavement, and when

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:42.510
I go inside she acts like I don't even exist.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:46.530
I shout at her, and I shake her, but nothing
works.

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:49.650
She just walks around me like I'm not there.

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:51.580
I scream at her for hours.

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:54.639
Hours! and she just ignores me.

00:07:54.639 --> 00:08:00.230
Every time I touch her she gets that disgusted
look on her face, like I'm some scum.

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:01.230
So I took it off forever.

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:04.310
She’s a backstabber and a liar.

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:05.560
She had it coming.

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:06.950
She got what she deserved.”

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:09.780
“Why didn't she just love me anymore?”

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:12.680
Daniel was just as confused as the SCP Foundation.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:18.550
He lost his relationship, the love of his
life, for no reason, and now he can’t even

00:08:18.550 --> 00:08:22.510
talk to her as he’s just met with silence
and a blank stare.

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:27.620
There was seemingly no answer, and the SCP
Foundation researchers were lost as to where

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:28.870
to start.

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:33.180
After a few days of scratching their heads,
researchers recalled the tick they removed

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:34.570
from Daniel’s neck.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:40.020
As weird as entertaining a tick as the possible
culprit of a bad break up may seem - Remember,

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:44.470
this is the SCP Foundation and they have people
running around in there obsessed with the

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:48.970
idea of eating bread in hopes to poop out
toast because they think they’re a toaster

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:52.269
for 343’s sake!

00:08:52.269 --> 00:08:54.709
Anyway…back to the tick.

00:08:54.709 --> 00:09:00.040
The SCP Foundation began testing on it and
just as their hunch suggested, it turned out

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:04.139
that it was far from a common tick, it merely
resembled one.

00:09:04.139 --> 00:09:08.110
The tick is now designated SCP-1655.

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:14.449
The Foundation also found something incredibly
peculiar, SCP-1655 does not follow the common

00:09:14.449 --> 00:09:19.389
life cycle of a normal tick and it does not
require the normal sustenance a non-anomalous

00:09:19.389 --> 00:09:21.779
tick of its species would need to survive.

00:09:21.779 --> 00:09:24.610
They found the specimen to be extremely aggressive.

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:29.949
It will immediately target the nearest mammal,
whether it be a small animal or a full grown

00:09:29.949 --> 00:09:35.670
human, SCP-1655 will latch itself onto their
body and begin drawing blood.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:40.700
Given how dangerous this anomaly could be
if not properly contained within safe parameters,

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:45.199
the SCP Foundation assigned it to the Euclid
level of containment classes.

00:09:45.199 --> 00:09:51.890
To ensure that SCP-1655 does not attach itself
to anyone of real importance at the SCP Foundation,

00:09:51.890 --> 00:09:55.110
the following containment procedures were
devised.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:10:01.240
SCP-1655 will be kept in a 5 x 5 x 5 cm plexiglass
container.

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:07.319
Importantly, any handling of SCP-1655 that
requires the opening of its container is to

00:10:07.319 --> 00:10:10.279
be performed by D-class personnel only.

00:10:10.279 --> 00:10:13.620
Guess that D does really stand for disposable,
huh.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:18.760
While the Foundation suspected SCP-1655 as
being the culprit for the seemingly anomalous

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:24.240
effects that ended with Daniel and Eliza breaking
up, they needed to run some tests to be sure

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:28.959
that SCP-1655 was in fact the danger they
thought it was.

00:10:28.959 --> 00:10:32.480
The first test began with a female tabby cat
and its kitten.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:36.619
The kitten was placed in its own chamber with
SCP-1655.

00:10:36.619 --> 00:10:39.810
In mere seconds, the tick latched onto the
young cat.

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:43.689
The kitten was then placed in the same testing
chamber as its mother and the mother cat no

00:10:43.689 --> 00:10:46.279
longer acknowledged the kitten's existence.

00:10:46.279 --> 00:10:50.600
The kitten meowed and cried for its mother’s
attention, however, no signs of recognition

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:52.529
were observed from the mother cat.

00:10:52.529 --> 00:10:56.839
Later, the kitten's attempts to feed from
its mother were also met with resistance.

00:10:56.839 --> 00:11:01.259
Because of this, the kitten was not able to
get enough sustenance, and thus starved to

00:11:01.259 --> 00:11:02.259
death.

00:11:02.259 --> 00:11:04.899
Researchers also found another odd feature
about SCP-1655.

00:11:04.899 --> 00:11:11.779
A viscous, plasma-like substance appeared
in SCP-1655's blood sack.

00:11:11.779 --> 00:11:16.260
Another test was conducted, this time on a
D-Class subject.

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:19.879
SCP-1655 was introduced to D-236.

00:11:19.879 --> 00:11:25.079
After a period of a few hours, D-236 was asked
to contact his grandmother who raised him

00:11:25.079 --> 00:11:27.779
from the age of 5 years old and on.

00:11:27.779 --> 00:11:32.939
When on the phone, D-236’s grandmother did
not appear to recognize or even hear D-236’s

00:11:32.939 --> 00:11:34.670
voice.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:39.369
The overseeing researcher then took the phone
and began to question D-236’s grandmother

00:11:39.369 --> 00:11:41.439
about D-236.

00:11:41.439 --> 00:11:45.730
The old woman didn’t understand what the
researcher was talking about and had no memories

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:46.730
of D-236.

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:53.329
SCP Foundation researchers then assigned a
meeting between D-236 and his grandmother.

00:11:53.329 --> 00:11:57.300
Upon meeting, the old woman showed no sign
of acknowledgement towards her grandson.

00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:01.180
A researcher asked D-236 to touch his grandmother
on the arm.

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:06.220
He reached out toward her and she immediately
recoiled with a look of disdain on her face,

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:07.390
but looking right through him.

00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:10.310
“What do you feel, ma’am” A researcher
asked the old woman.

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:14.209
“I don’t know – It’s like something
spooky or something.”

00:12:14.209 --> 00:12:19.730
Over the period of the meeting, D-236 grew
extremely emotionally distressed and had to

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:22.350
be removed from the meeting location.

00:12:22.350 --> 00:12:28.899
Notably, SCP-1655 appeared engorged following
this meeting, as if it was filled with blood.

00:12:28.899 --> 00:12:33.540
From these tests, the SCP Foundation and its
researchers were able to devise the following

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:39.040
list of phenomena that will occur when SCP-1655
latches to a subject.

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:40.040
1.

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:44.120
Any living being the affected subject held
any degree of affection for will immediately

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:47.040
lose all memory of the subject's existence.

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:49.730
This includes minor interactions to life-long
relationships.

00:12:49.730 --> 00:12:55.740
The people who once knew the victim will also
be unable to create or acquire any new memories

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:58.930
concerning the victim or anything surrounding
them.

00:12:58.930 --> 00:12:59.930
2.

00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:05.029
People who were once connected to the subject
will not be able to sense the victim of SCP-1655

00:13:05.029 --> 00:13:07.529
in any manner no matter the circumstance.

00:13:07.529 --> 00:13:13.430
However, any physical contact with the victim
of SCP-1655 will cause mild discomfort and

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:14.470
disgust.

00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:19.449
If the physical contact is left for a prolonged
period of time, discomfort and disgust will

00:13:19.449 --> 00:13:25.269
increase in intensity the longer contact is
held until the physical contact is removed.

00:13:25.269 --> 00:13:26.269
3.

00:13:26.269 --> 00:13:30.209
If the subject begins to feel affection for
any other living being, including animals

00:13:30.209 --> 00:13:36.680
or other humans, they will also be affected
by SCP-1655 and its anomalous properties.

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:42.759
SCP Foundation researcher’s hypothesize
that SCP-1655 is able to extract information

00:13:42.759 --> 00:13:44.149
from its victims.

00:13:44.149 --> 00:13:50.619
In turn, SCP-1655 has the ability to alter
its effects thus allowing it to maintain complete

00:13:50.619 --> 00:13:56.449
emotional isolation on its victims and, in
turn, feed on more of these negative emotions

00:13:56.449 --> 00:13:59.129
that it causes its victims to have.

00:13:59.129 --> 00:14:00.129
4.

00:14:00.129 --> 00:14:04.999
The subject will ignore SCP-1655's existence.

00:14:04.999 --> 00:14:08.739
Possibly the most important detail of the
SCP Foundation’s findings are about the

00:14:08.739 --> 00:14:14.790
lingering effects of SCP-1655, even after
it was removed from a victim.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:19.220
It was found that these effects of being unable
to create human connections remain permanent

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:24.199
well after removal, however, anyone the victim
is not affectionate towards is not affected

00:14:24.199 --> 00:14:31.490
by SCP-1655’s effects, but if that connection
is made, the victim practically does not exist

00:14:31.490 --> 00:14:33.019
to that person.

00:14:33.019 --> 00:14:37.550
SCP Foundation researchers hypothesize that
the parasite keeps a mental link with its

00:14:37.550 --> 00:14:38.630
victims.

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:43.470
It then continues to feed off of the negative
emotions the effects of its bite has placed

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:44.579
on the victim.

00:14:44.579 --> 00:14:51.309
It makes sense why the SCP Foundation researchers
made such strict special containment procedures

00:14:51.309 --> 00:14:52.670
for SCP-1655.

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:56.759
Something undetectable that completely and
mindlessly eliminates human connection is

00:14:56.759 --> 00:15:00.630
extremely dangerous if it’s allowed to be
left uncontained.

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:06.360
The SCP Foundation researchers then began
testing on SCP-1655’s saliva and the fluid

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:09.100
it was putting into the bloodstream of its
victims.

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:12.980
Unfortunately, the tests were unable to identify
all of the different components.

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:18.449
There were, however, powerful depressant chemicals
and traces of hormones found that can negatively

00:15:18.449 --> 00:15:21.719
affect the Hippocampus section of a victim’s
brain.

00:15:21.719 --> 00:15:26.129
The hippocampus is the area of the brain located
in the temporal lobe.

00:15:26.129 --> 00:15:30.069
It is responsible for learning and acts as
a storage unit for memory.

00:15:30.069 --> 00:15:36.429
And SCP-1655 appears to extract memories from
its victim’s hippocampus using these unknown

00:15:36.429 --> 00:15:41.259
hormones, causing the people surrounding the
victim to completely detach from them.

00:15:41.259 --> 00:15:45.930
Could it be possible that SCP-1655 has telepathic
abilities?

00:15:45.930 --> 00:15:52.329
While physiological examinations proved unable
to confirm how SCP-1655 uses the information

00:15:52.329 --> 00:15:57.619
it retrieves from the Hippocampus to affect
others, it is extremely clear that it is actively

00:15:57.619 --> 00:16:03.069
causing mental anguish to its subjects, most
likely in order to speed up its feeding process.

00:16:03.069 --> 00:16:08.769
So it’s definitely clear that SCP-1655 feeds
off the turmoil it inflicts.

00:16:08.769 --> 00:16:12.249
But the larger questions are why and how?

00:16:12.249 --> 00:16:16.139
How did SCP-1655 develop these abilities?

00:16:16.139 --> 00:16:17.339
Was it evolution?

00:16:17.339 --> 00:16:19.810
Perhaps that is in fact the case here.

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:21.720
Or maybe it’s even simpler.

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:26.319
Maybe the tick lacked a sustainable food source
and just decided to feed on something else

00:16:26.319 --> 00:16:31.069
that was easily accessible and just as sustainable:
Negativity.

00:16:31.069 --> 00:16:35.940
So we have an entity that eliminates all human
bonds from the person it attaches to, then

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:40.249
it takes the pain and anguish a person feels
from their emotional connections disappearing

00:16:40.249 --> 00:16:42.050
to sustain itself.

00:16:42.050 --> 00:16:46.889
Very dangerous stuff here that, if left to
the wild, could cause unimaginable damage.

00:16:46.889 --> 00:16:54.139
Imagine if this was left in a large city,
allowing SCP-1655 to jump from person to person,

00:16:54.139 --> 00:16:58.430
eliminating each person’s emotional connections
until there is nothing left.

00:16:58.430 --> 00:17:03.440
The damage could potentially cause a Broken
Masquerade scenario for the SCP Foundation.

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:08.550
These scenarios occur when the SCP Foundation
is unable to properly contain an anomaly and

00:17:08.550 --> 00:17:11.810
thus, knowledge of the anomalous world becomes
public.

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:18.800
Among their research into SCP-1655’s biology,
yet another interesting part of SCP-1655 was

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:19.800
found.

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:23.209
It’s a female specimen and has the necessary
reproductive organs.

00:17:23.209 --> 00:17:29.280
While this may seem mundane, this means that
SCP-1655 may have been capable of laying eggs

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:35.920
in the wild, implying that other members of
SCP-1655’s species may be out in the wild,

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:41.510
waiting to attach itself to unknowing humans
and expand their relationship-ruining reach.

00:17:41.510 --> 00:17:45.340
Further investigation has been recommended
by the overseeing researchers.

00:17:45.340 --> 00:17:50.740
The SCP Foundation runs into anomalies of
all shapes, sizes and danger levels.

00:17:50.740 --> 00:17:57.080
Some anomalies may seem rather mundane, but
pose danger when put into very specific circumstances.

00:17:57.080 --> 00:18:01.310
In the case of ticks in general, they have
been responsible for feeding on human flesh

00:18:01.310 --> 00:18:03.440
and spreading diseases for ages.

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:09.900
But now, with SCP-1655 in the game it seems
that some of the species have turned to feeding

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:12.690
on more than just our tangible parts.

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:16.630
Remember earlier when I mentioned that human
connection is what allowed for humans to become

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:17.660
the dominant species?

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:24.210
Well there’s a whole lot of us humans running
around, and if there are SCP-1655 species

00:18:24.210 --> 00:18:28.350
mating and spreading among us, it won’t
be too long until our reign in the animal

00:18:28.350 --> 00:18:31.410
kingdom comes to a blood-sucking end.

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:36.830
Just when we thought losing Wifi connection
was annoying - Imagine losing all Human connection?

00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:37.830
Yikes!

00:18:37.830 --> 00:18:44.750
Now go check out “SCP-2031 - Ant Farm”
and “Reconstructive Maggots - SCP-726”

00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:49.120
for more anomalies of the creepy crawly nature
from SCP Explained!

